# Module layout

Every feature module keeps this tree. Do not add `services/`, `helpers/`, or `utils/` inside a module.

```text
controllers/ → dto/ → application/ → domain/ + repositories/
                                   ↑
                              policies/
```

- `controllers/` — HTTP only. One controller. Parse, call one application function, map errors.
- `dto/` — one file per request body. Parse and validate. No class-validator.
- `application/` — one use case per file. Only layer that calls repositories.
- `domain/` — pure rules. No Mongo, no HTTP.
- `repositories/` — Mongo only. Multi-document writes use `runInTransaction`.
- `schemas/` — document type and collection name. One collection per file.
- `policies/` — who may act. Resolve membership on the server. Ignore a role sent by the client.
- `tests/` — that module only.

File names are kebab-case. The module class stays at `<name>.module.ts`. Use `policies/` only for auth guards and workspace checks.
